{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>I said.</b> After I wondered how it could be that it is the deed of Elohim, I knew that Elohim will judge the righteous and the wicked. The sense of \"there\" alludes to the world to come, just as \"and the crafty I return there\" alludes to the place of the grave. And if he returns there to the earth from which he was taken, he will return — this matter too, after death."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:24.162930400Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}